  "question": {
    "text": "Consider circles&nbsp;<math><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> touching both the axes and passing through <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math> then the&nbsp;<math><mi>x</mi></math>-intercept of the common chord of the circles is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "8",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Since the circle touches both the axes and passes through <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, it lies in the first quadrant, so its equation is<br /><math><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> lies on it, hence<br /><math><msup><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>16</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>⇒</mo><msub><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></math><br /><math><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> is <math><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></math><br /><math><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is <math><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></math><br />Equation of the common chord is<br /><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math></p><p>Hence, the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-intercept is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn></math>&nbsp;</p>",
